Unisciti alla nostra organizzazione e diventa:

M&A Deal Analytics Associate

All'interno della nostra unità organizzativa Transaction Services, il team M&A Deal Analytics opera all'intersezione tra M&A, Financial Due Diligence e advanced analytics. Supportiamo investitori corporate e private equity, management team e altri advisor nelle fasi più decisive del ciclo di vita di un deal — buy-side, sell-side, vendor assistance e exit readiness — trasformando grandi volumi di dati finanziari, operativi e commerciali in insight chiari e azionabili che rafforzano l'equity story, supportano le decisioni di investimento e danno ai nostri clienti maggiore fiducia nelle decisioni strategiche legate al deal.

Your Perspectives

Siamo alla ricerca di una risorsa che entri a far parte del team M&A Deal Analytics e contribuisca attivamente alle seguenti attività:
• Analizzare i principali driver di ricavi, margini e KPI operativi delle società target per identificare trend, rischi e leve di valore a supporto delle ipotesi di investimento e della costruzione dell'equity story;
• Supporto al team Transaction Service Core nella quantificazione e discussione di aggiustamenti di quality of earnings, normalized EBITDA, working capital e net debt partendo da dataset complessi;
• Estrarre, riconciliare e trasformare dati provenienti da sistemi gestionali (ERP, CRM, billing), database finanziari e fonti pubbliche, garantendo la coerenza con i management accounts e la documentazione di due diligence;
• Costruire dashboard dinamiche, databook e presentazioni di elevata qualità per comunicare le analisi in modo efficace a C-level, deal team e investitori — traducendo la complessità dei dati in una narrativa transazionale chiara;
• Interagire trasversalmente con il cliente e con altre service line, contribuendo a deliverable integrati che abbracciano l'intero ciclo del deal;
• Esplorare l'utilizzo di tecniche di intelligenza artificiale e advanced analytics per rispondere alle domande di business più complesse e sviluppare nuovi servizi a valore aggiunto per i clienti.

Your unique strengths

Formazione e background
• Sei in possesso o stai per conseguire una laurea magistrale in Economia, Finanza, Ingegneria Gestionale, Statistica, Matematica o discipline affini, con una solida base quantitativa e una chiara comprensione dei fondamentali di corporate finance;
• Un'esperienza di 6–12 mesi in Financial Due Diligence, Transaction Services, M&A advisory, investment banking, audit o ruoli analoghi presso primarie società di consulenza o istituzioni finanziarie sarà considerata un plus significativo;
Mindset e competenze professionali
• Hai curiosità commerciale: capisci come le aziende generino valore, e sai collegare l'analisi dei dati alle dinamiche di un deal — valutazione, negoziazione, strutturazione dell'operazione;
• Hai spiccate capacità analitiche e di problem solving, con attenzione al dettaglio e un approccio strutturato e metodico;
• Sai comunicare risultati e insight in modo chiaro ed efficace sia a interlocutori tecnici sia a stakeholder non tecnici, con un approccio da consulente;
• Hai un'ottima attitudine al lavoro in team e ti trovi a tuo agio in contesti dinamici, con deadline serrate e progetti multipli in parallelo;
• Parli e scrivi in inglese fluentemente, preferibilmente grazie ad esperienze di studio o lavoro internazio [...]

Are you ready to shape the future with confidence?

Here at EY, you’ll have the chance to build a truly exceptional experience. We’ll empower you with the latest technology, surround you with high-performing teams, and provide the global scale and diverse and inclusive culture you need to discover your full potential. Through our coaching and training programs, you’ll develop the skills you need to stay relevant today and, in the future, – all while building a network of colleagues, mentors, and leaders who will be on the journey with you at EY and beyond.

The opportunity: your next adventure awaits

EY is a global professional services organization providing advisory, assurance, tax and transaction advisory services. We are committed to doing our part in building a better working world for our people, our clients and our communities. And we are united by our shared values and a dedication to delivering exceptional client service.

At EY, we support you in achieving your unique potential — both personally and professionally. We give you stretching and rewarding experiences that keep you motivated, working in an atmosphere of integrity and teaming with some of the world’s most successful companies. And while we encourage you to take personal responsibility for your career, we support you in your professional development in every way we can. You enjoy the flexibility to devote time to what matters to you, in your business and personal lives. At EY you can be who you are and express your point of view, energy, and enthusiasm, wherever you are in the world. It’s how you make a difference.

In order to continue the expansion of our Financial Services practice, we are currently looking to recruit an Intern for our Valuation Team in FAAS (Financial Accounting and Advisory Services). (f/m).

Your mission

As an Intern, your responsibilities will be to perform and carry out analyses of valuation of different assets types (e.g. Private Equity, Private Debt). You will be supporting the team in assessing the reasonableness of valuations and financial models in the context of financial reporting and assurance related engagements.

Preferred knowledge/skills

- Student from an economics, business and/or management school with a focus in finance and/or accounting;

- Theoretical and practical knowledge of valuation principles (market approach, income approach,…);

- Strong analytical skills, problem solver, detail-oriented, entrepreneurial;

- Enjoying working in a multi-cultural environment;

- Ability to manage multiple threads of tasks and / or engagements;

- Outstanding organizational skills, flexibility and ability to work under tight deadlines;

- Perfect command of English, both written and verbally, within a professional services business environment;

- Command of French or German language is an asset and additional language would be considered as a plus;

- PC proficiency including MS Excel, Word, and PowerPoint;

What we offer

- Continuous learning: You’ll develop the mindset and skills to navigate whatever comes next.

- Success as defined by you: We’ll provide the tools and flexibility, so you can make a meaningful impact, your way.

- Transformative leadership: We’ll give you the insights, coaching and confidence to be the leader the world needs.

- Diverse and inclusive culture: You’ll be embraced for who you are and empowered to use your voice to help others find theirs.

EY | Building a better working world

