Client Relationship Management Analyst – Trade Credit Insurance
Dubai | UAE National

We are looking for a proactive and relationship-oriented individual to join our Trade Credit Insurance practice in Dubai.
This is an excellent opportunity to build a career in a client- and market-facing environment. You will work closely with experienced colleagues while developing relationships with clients, insurers and underwriters. As your knowledge and experience grow, you will progressively take ownership of your own client portfolio.

What you will do

- Support the team with the day-to-day management of an existing client portfolio;

- Assist with operational processes, including revenue booking, quote comparisons, claims-related matters and risk information requests;

- Help prepare client documentation, reports and presentations;

- Communicate with clients, insurers and underwriters and build effective working relationships across the market;

- Work with senior team members to understand client needs and deliver timely, high-quality support;

- Participate in relevant client, insurer and team meetings and events;

- Learn and use the team’s systems, digital tools and AI-enabled solutions;

- Gradually develop the knowledge and confidence required to manage your own portfolio of clients.

What we are looking for

- UAE national;

- Currently based in Dubai;

- Bachelor’s degree, preferably in Business Administration or a related field;

- Relevant professional experience or an internship involving client interaction, relationship management or business support would be advantageous;

- Strong communication and interpersonal skills;

- A genuine interest in working with clients and developing commercial relationships;

- A proactive approach, curiosity and willingness to learn;

- Ability to take ownership and work collaboratively within a team;

- Basic proficiency in Microsoft Excel and PowerPoint;

- Confidence in learning new systems and digital tools.

We are open to both high-potential graduates and candidates with relevant early-career experience.

Marsh Risk is a business of Marsh (NYSE: MRSH), a global leader in risk, reinsurance and capital, people and investments, and management consulting, advising clients in 130 countries. With annual revenue of over $27 billion and more than 95,000 colleagues, Marsh helps build the confidence to thrive through the power of perspective. For more information about Marsh Risk, visit marsh.com, or follow us on LinkedIn and X.

Marsh is committed to embracing a diverse, inclusive and flexible work environment. We aim to attract and retain the best people and embrace diversity of age, background, disability, ethnic origin, family duties, nationality, parental status, personal or social status, political affiliation, race, religion and beliefs, sex/gender, skin color, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.

Marsh is committed to hybrid work, which includes the flexibility of working remotely and the collaboration, connections and professional development benefits of working together in the office. All Marsh colleagues are expected to be in their local office or working onsite with clients at least three days per week. Office-based teams will identify at least one “anchor day” per week on which their full team will be together in person.

Operating as an internationally integrated partnership in over 100 countries and territories, Forvis Mazars Group specialises in audit, tax and advisory services. The partnership draws on the expertise and cultural understanding of over 40,000 professionals across the globe to assist clients of all sizes at every stage in their development.

Wir suchen mehrere engagierte, dynamische und motivierte Studierende, die unser Audit-Team ab Januar 2027 verstärken möchten.

Deine Aufgaben
Als Praktikant*in in der Wirtschaftsprüfung wirst du:

- Die verantwortlichen Prüfer*innen bei der Erstellung und Dokumentation von Prüfungsunterlagen unterstützen;

- Die dir zugewiesenen Prüfungshandlungen verstehen und selbstständig durchführen;

- Die Prüfungsmethodik, den Audit-Ansatz sowie die Tools von Forvis Mazars kennenlernen und anwenden;

- Während deiner Mission von erfahrenen Senior Auditors und Manager*innen begleitet und geschult werden;

- An Prüfungsmandaten in verschiedenen Branchen mitwirken, darunter Banken und PSF, Handels- und Industrieunternehmen, Versicherungen und Rückversicherungen, Investmentfonds sowie Private Equity und Immobiliengesellschaften.

Dein Profil

- Du absolvierst derzeit ein Masterstudium mit Schwerpunkt Wirtschaftsprüfung, Rechnungswesen oder Finanzen;

- Erste Erfahrungen im Bereich Rechnungswesen, Wirtschaftsprüfung, Controlling oder in einem ähnlichen Bereich sind von Vorteil;

- Du verfügst über sehr gute Deutsch- und Englischkenntnisse. Weitere Sprachkenntnisse sind ein Plus;

- Du bist motiviert, proaktiv, lernbereit und arbeitest gerne im Team;

- Du verfügst über gute Kommunikations- und Sozialkompetenzen;

- Du bist bereit, ein Vollzeitpraktikum von mindestens sechs Monaten zu absolvieren;

- Eine von deiner Hochschule ausgestellte Praktikumsvereinbarung ist erforderlich.

Wir bieten dir
Bei Forvis Mazars hast du die Möglichkeit:

- In einem jungen, dynamischen und kollegialen Arbeitsumfeld zu arbeiten;

- Wertvolle Praxiserfahrung mit einer vielfältigen Mandantschaft zu sammeln, von börsennotierten Konzernen bis hin zu kleinen und mittleren Unternehmen;

- Fachkenntnisse in Bereichen wie Banking & PSF, Commercial Companies, Insurance, Investment Funds, Private Equity oder Real Estate aufzubauen;

- Von einem strukturierten Einarbeitungs- und Schulungsprogramm zu profitieren, um unsere Methodik kennenzulernen und technisches Fachwissen zu den Rechnungslegungsstandards sowie zum luxemburgischen Rechtsumfeld zu erwerben.

Nach erfolgreichem Abschluss deines Praktikums besteht die Möglichkeit, als Junior Auditor bei Forvis Mazars einzusteigen.

Forvis Mazars is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to building a diverse and inclusive culture in which each individual feels welcomed.
We consider candidates based on their skills, abilities or experiences as we believe everyone brings their own talents with them.

The diversity of our talents is what makes our work environment multicultural, innovative and enriching.

A career at Lombard Odier means working for a renowned global wealth and asset manager, with a strong focus on sustainable investing. An innovative bank of choice for private and institutional clients, our independently owned Firm is one of the best-capitalised banking groups in the world, managing close to CHF 300 billion and operating from over 25 offices across 4 continents.

With a history spanning over 230 years, Lombard Odier is an investment house providing a comprehensive offering of discretionary and advisory portfolio management, wealth services and custody. We also offer asset management services and investment strategies through Lombard Odier Investment Managers and provide advanced banking technology to other financial institutions.

“Rethink Everything” is our philosophy – it is at the heart of everything we do. We have grown stronger through more than 40 financial crises by rethinking the world around us to provide a fresh investment perspective for our clients.

Huissier-ère sécurité (Genève, Suisse)

VOTRE MISSION :

- Garantir la sécurité physique des personnes et la protection des biens ;

- Assurer les missions de sûreté et de surveillance ;

- Intervenir en cas d’alarme incendie, sûreté et sanitaire ;

- Détecter les dangers en amont dans le cadre de la sécurité et les gérer ;

- Estimer les situations pouvant entraîner un disfonctionnement de sécurité et prendre les mesures adéquates ;

- Dispenser et suivre des formations dans les domaines informatiques, techniques et sécurité ;

- Intervenir, suivre, et gérer les différents outils techniques en matière de sécurité et de sûreté ;

- Gérer les tâches administratives du service de sécurité ;

- Assurer des missions spécifiques au service de sécurité in ou hors du site ;

- Assurer un service de piquet.

VOTRE PROFIL :

- CFC technique ou formation équivalente ;

- Le brevet fédéral d’Agent de Sécurité et Surveillance (ASS) est un atout ;

- Une formation dans les domaines du feu et/ou sanitaire ;

- Expériences et références dans le domaine de la sécurité et de la sûreté ;

- De langue maternelle française avec de très bonnes connaissances de l’anglais (orales et écrites) ;

- Maîtrise des systèmes informatiques usuels et techniques en matière de sécurité physique (SAE, SCA, Reporting, etc.) ;

- Moralité irréprochable, esprit d’équipe, dynamique ;

